DTSTART:2026-02-26T23:30:00+00:00
DTEND:2026-02-27T02:30:00+00:00
SUMMARY:Free Food/Stuff @ Dinner &  A Movie : Wicked: For Good
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy dinner, a backstage tour of Braden Auditorium, and Wicked: For Good!

Limit 150 participants. Admission is first come, first serve. No RSVP required. RSVP does not guarantee participation.

Doors Open & Optional Tour of Braden Auditorium Backstage: 5:30 p.m.

Dinner Served & Movie Begins: 6 P.M.

Menu: Baked Potato Bar

If you need accommodation to fully participate in this program/event, please contact Event Management, Dining, and Hospitality at 309-438-8351 or EMDH@IllinoisState.edu. Please allow sufficient time to arrange the accommodation.
LOCATION:Braden Auditorium, Bone Student Center
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:10e7ea63-053f-49e3-b1f9-325cfc57ccc0
DTSTAMP:20260223T191723Z
DTSTART:2026-02-27T18:00:00+00:00
DTEND:2026-02-27T19:00:00+00:00
SUMMARY:Free Food @ Conversations Café
DESCRIPTION:Conversations Café
🕛 12:00 – 1:00 PM
📍 OIE Lobby, 2nd Floor Fell Hall

Join us for the Conversations Café, a cozy, coffee shop–style gathering hosted by the OIE I-House and Academic Teams. This program offers a welcoming space for students to connect, unwind, and engage in global conversations.

Enjoy:
✅ Coffee, tea, and snacks from a featured country
✅ Board games and friendly, global conversations
✅ A craft table and stress-relief activities
✅ A calm, inclusive atmosphere

Whether you want to practice your English, learn about different cultures, meet new people, or take a break from a busy week, this is the perfect place to relax and recharge.

All students are welcome—no RSVP necessary!
LOCATION:Fell Hall, Second Floor Lobby
END:VEVENT
