BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1ab5f782-8fcf-4a3e-908d-5090d5d3a9ea
DTSTAMP:20260223T191723Z
DTSTART:2026-03-05T00:30:00+00:00
DTEND:2026-03-05T01:30:00+00:00
SUMMARY:Free Food @ ACM - Meeting #7, Movie Night: The Internet's Own Boy (2014)
DESCRIPTION:Join the ACM for a movie night, where we'll be watching "The Internet's Own Boy (2014)", a documentary about programming prodigy and information activist Aaron Swartz. *Note: An RSVP is required, for pizza ordering purposes.

Movie Description: "He helped develop the Internet Protocol RSS and was a co-founder of Reddit. Chronicling his pioneering efforts crusading for open access and free speech and the resulting legal nightmare and tragedy that ensued, The Internet's Own Boy is a dynamic and moving portrait of a brilliant tech millionaire who renounced the values of Silicon Valley startup culture and used technology to tirelessly fight for social justice, no matter what the cost."

Perks:

- Fun Technology Movie

- Pizza

- ACM
LOCATION:Julian Hall, Room 31
END:VEVENT
